Uploaded PDF
Redesign the attached PDF into a completely new, highly professional BTech final-year project report.

This is a DESIGN REVISION of the attached PDF, not a new document from an unrelated topic.

PRIMARY REQUIREMENTS

1. Preserve all useful factual content from the attached PDF.
2. Do not omit, shorten, summarize, or duplicate the source content.
3. Remove accidental repeated chapters, duplicate paragraphs, broken sections, raw Markdown, internal instructions, placeholders, and malformed tables.
4. Correct the complete document hierarchy, heading numbering, chapter order, table numbering, figure numbering, equation numbering, and table of contents.
5. Automatically understand the document’s subject, audience, content density, mathematics, data, diagrams, tables, and technical depth.
6. Automatically select the best professional architecture from the available architecture library.
7. If no existing architecture fits properly, synthesize a new best-fit architecture using validated professional components.
8. Do not ask me to choose a template, theme, layout, or architecture.

DESIGN DIRECTION

Create a modern engineering and academic design suitable for:

- a BTech student;
- final-year project submission;
- faculty evaluation;
- technical presentation;
- professional portfolio use;
- comfortable screen reading;
- high-quality printing.

The document should look professionally designed by an experienced academic publication and engineering-document design team.

Use:

- clean academic typography;
- strong information hierarchy;
- balanced white space;
- restrained professional visual styling;
- consistent spacing;
- readable text size;
- polished tables;
- clear diagrams;
- professional equations;
- meaningful charts;
- page-specific layouts.

Do not use a single repeated page frame throughout the document.

Use different page architectures where appropriate:

- minimal professional cover;
- clean contents page;
- executive overview;
- chapter opener;
- normal reading page;
- two-column explanation page;
- technical architecture page;
- workflow diagram page;
- wide comparison-table page;
- mathematical analysis page;
- chart and interpretation page;
- risk-matrix page;
- implementation-roadmap page;
- recommendation page;
- conclusion page;
- references and appendix pages.

COVER PAGE

Create a completely redesigned minimal professional cover.

The cover must show only the real document title derived from the source subject.

Never use these as the title:

- User
- Assistant
- Serenya
- PDF Document
- Professional PDF
- Create a PDF
- Redesign this PDF
- Final PDF Generation Instruction

Do not automatically add:

- logo;
- Authentic AI name;
- generated-by text;
- watermark;
- author;
- date;
- document-type label;
- cover statistics;
- decorative metadata.

CONTENT ARCHITECTURE

Rebuild the document into one canonical structure.

Ensure:

- every section appears only once;
- no chapter is repeated later in the PDF;
- table of contents matches the final canonical structure;
- no artificial labels such as SECTION 01, SECTION 27, or SECTION 88 appear;
- missing heading levels are repaired;
- headings are not orphaned at the bottom of pages;
- paragraphs are not unnecessarily split;
- lists are correctly formatted;
- no Markdown symbols such as ###, ####, pipes, or extraction markers remain visible.

MATHEMATICAL INTELLIGENCE

Detect every formula, equation, numerical model, percentage, cost calculation, performance comparison, and quantitative claim.

For supported mathematical content:

- normalize mathematical symbols;
- use professional equation notation;
- define variables;
- preserve units;
- show formulas clearly;
- substitute available values;
- solve calculations step by step;
- verify the numerical result independently;
- identify missing variables;
- never invent missing values;
- clearly distinguish exact results, approximate results, assumptions, and illustrative data.

Place relevant equations, calculations, tables, and graphs together on coherent mathematical-analysis pages.

DATA AND CHARTS

Where the source contains sufficient numerical data:

- create actual professional charts;
- do not print instructions such as “Suggested visual”;
- use readable axis labels;
- include units;
- avoid label overlap;
- show current-versus-target comparisons;
- calculate and display reductions where supported;
- include a concise analytical interpretation;
- state clearly when values are illustrative planning assumptions.

Never fabricate chart data.

TABLES

Reconstruct all malformed tables.

Requirements:

- proper rows and columns;
- readable cell text;
- no raw pipe syntax;
- no extraction markers;
- no mid-word splitting;
- no clipped columns;
- repeat table headings across continuation pages;
- use landscape orientation automatically for wide tables;
- keep captions and explanatory notes with their tables.

DIAGRAMS

Where supported by the source, create clear professional diagrams for:

- system architecture;
- workflow stages;
- data movement;
- approval flow;
- execution boundaries;
- implementation phases.

Do not invent unsupported technical components.

QUALITY RULES

Before delivering the revised PDF, validate every page for:

- incorrect title;
- duplicate content;
- raw Markdown;
- internal-instruction leakage;
- placeholder text;
- broken equations;
- missing requested charts;
- graph-label overlap;
- malformed tables;
- clipped content;
- extremely small text;
- inconsistent headings;
- incorrect table of contents;
- unnecessary blank pages;
- excessive empty space;
- repeated headers or footers;
- artificial section labels.

Automatically reflow and repair any page that fails validation.

OUTPUT RULES

- No fixed page-count limit.
- Allow the document to use as many pages as required by its content.
- Do not reduce font size merely to reduce page count.
- Do not remove content to fit an arbitrary limit.
- Do not add branding.
- Do not add a watermark.
- Do not add repeated headers or footers.
- Do not add visible page numbers unless they are explicitly required by the source.
- Do not print these instructions inside the document.
- Preserve source-supported meaning and technical accuracy.

Generate the final redesigned PDF as:

AI-Enabled-University-Operations-Redesigned.pdf

